.com/jonochocki/mission-control/commit/69cdf7f3a87df8204bba8dce691150a71375f124","sha":"69cdf7f3a87df8204bba8dce691150a71375f124","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/commits/69cdf7f3a87df8204bba8dce691150a71375f124"}],"sha":"6dbf824738d950bd06a1414fe9b3bcad415e8591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/commits/6dbf824738d950bd06a1414fe9b3bcad415e8591"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/commits/6188cc492651acae78a5d8e5dac45324c69f455b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T06:40:16Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T06:40:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve open issue/PR backlog (security audits + fixes + apiFetch migration) (#723)\n\n* fix(command): return actionable error on ENOENT spawn failure (#588)\n\nWhen a runtime binary (openclaw/clawdbot) is missing from PATH, surface a\nfriendly message naming the missing command and the *_BIN override env var\ninstead of a raw ''spawn ENOENT''.\n\n* docs: refresh README screenshots and ignore docs/_*.png debug artifacts\n\n* fix(build): pin pnpm to v10 and complete onlyBuiltDependencies allowlist (#702)\n\npnpm 11 turns ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS into a hard error, breaking fresh\nDocker builds. Pin pnpm@10.29.3 via packageManager + Dockerfile (matching\nCI) and extend onlyBuiltDependencies to cover all native deps that ship\nbuild scripts (@parcel/watcher, @swc/core, esbuild, sharp, unrs-resolver).\n\nCloses #702. Supersedes #703, #705, #713.\n\n* fix(security): handle SecretRef-form gateway auth credentials (#670)\n\n/api/security-audit crashed with ''trim is not a function'' when\ngateway.auth.token/.password is a SecretRef object (vault/file-backed)\ninstead of a plain string. Add a hasCredential() typeguard that treats any\nnon-null value as configured; the resolved value is validated by OpenClaw\nat runtime. Adds a regression test covering string, empty, missing, and\nSecretRef forms.\n\nCloses #670. Supersedes #674 (NePav).\n\n* feat(api-client): add apiFetch with global 401/403/5xx handling (#681)\n\nAdds apiFetch<T>() (src/lib/api-client.ts) that sends cookies, redirects to\n/login on 401 (with a redirect-loop guard), and throws typed ApiError for\n403/404/5xx/network/parse failures. Mounts AuthExpiredListener at the root\nlayout and adds a warn-level eslint rule discouraging bare fetch(''/api/...'').\n\nReconstructed from PR #681 authored by jun261930-tech (the original branch was\ncut from a pre-hardening base, so it is re-applied here rather than merged).\nSecurity-audited + independently re-verified: same-origin only, sameSite=strict\ncookie can''t leak cross-origin, /login ''from'' param is inert (never read).\nDropped the non-functional TemplateLiteral eslint selector.\n\n* fix(ui): stop focus trap from stealing focus on re-render (#673)\n\nuseFocusTrap bundled initial-focus with the keydown-listener effect, keyed on\nthe recreated handleKeyDown. When a parent re-rendered (e.g. on every SSE\nupdate during task editing), the effect re-ran and refocused the first field,\nyanking the cursor from the description back to the title. Split into a\nmount-only focus/restore effect ([] deps) and a separate listener effect.\n\nCloses #673.\n\n* fix(gateway): negotiate protocol range 3..4 instead of pinning v3 (#701)\n\nThe connect handshake hardcoded PROTOCOL_VERSION=3 as both minProtocol and\nmaxProtocol, so OpenClaw 2026.5.18+ (which requires maxProtocol>=4) rejected\nthe handshake with ''protocol mismatch''. Advertise a [min,max] window (3..4) via\na testable buildProtocolNegotiation() helper in websocket-utils, staying\nbackward-compatible with v3-only gateways. Adds unit tests.\n\nCloses #701.\n\n* feat(tasks): auto-route unassigned tasks to coordinator agent (#663)\n\nMC_COORDINATOR_AGENT was documented but never consumed by task creation. Add\nconfig.coordinatorAgent (opt-in; empty = disabled) and a pure resolveTaskAssignee()\nhelper, then thread the resolved assignee through the INSERT, status\nnormalization, activity log, and assignment notification in POST /api/tasks.\nNew tasks created without an assignee now route to the coordinator when set.\n\nCloses #663.\n\n* fix(heartbeat): stop returning the same mentions on every poll (#662)\n\nThe heartbeat GET built a ''mentions'' work item from a raw comments query with\nonly a 4h time filter and no read-state, so the same mentions reappeared on\nevery poll for 4 hours. Comment creation already emits acknowledgeable\n''mention''-type notifications (surfaced by the unread-notifications work item),\nmaking that query redundant. Remove it; mentions are now acknowledged by\nmarking their notification read.\n\nCloses #662.\n\n* fix(spawn): fall back to modern agent method when sessions_spawn is gone (#645)\n\nOpenClaw 2026.5.x removed the sessions_spawn gateway method, so the Spawn\nbutton failed with ''unknown method: sessions_spawn''. Detect that error via a\nnew isUnknownMethodError() helper and fall back to the modern ''agent''\ninvocation (message param) that task-dispatch already uses. Reports which\nmethod was used in the audit log + response.\n\nCloses #645.\n\n* refactor: migrate 188 bare fetch(''/api/...'') sites to apiFetch (#682-#697)\n\nMigrate 21 components/panels from bare fetch to apiFetch<T>() so 401/403/5xx/\nnetwork failures are handled uniformly (401 redirects to /login; the rest throw\ntyped ApiError). Each call site preserves its original behavior: graceful-\ndegradation sites keep their try/catch swallow, server error messages are\nre-surfaced via ApiError.payload, and redundant Content-Type headers are\ndropped. Verified: 0 bare /api fetches remain, tsc clean, 964 unit tests pass,\nno new lint warnings.\n\nReconstructed from the apiFetch migration series by jun261930-tech (PRs\nmigration was re-derived on current main per-file). Fixes a latent bug in the\noriginal chat migration where conversation-list computed but never used its\nparsed sessions.\n\n* fix(tasks): correct comment-tab count and stop scroll reset on poll (#664, #660)\n\n#664: the comments-tab badge used comments.length (top-level threads only)\nwhile the task-card badge uses a flat COUNT(*) over all comments. Add a pure\ncountCommentsDeep() that recurses through replies so both badges agree.\n\n#660: fetchComments toggled loadingComments on every 15s background poll,\nunmounting the comment list and resetting the user''s scroll position. Gate the\nloading placeholder behind a first-load ref so the DOM stays mounted across\npolls; reset the guard when switching tasks.\n\nCloses #664, #660.\n\n* fix(chat): let users start conversations with registered agents (#611)\n\nThe chat conversation list never invoked its onNewConversation prop and only\nrendered gateway/local sessions, so when no sessions existed it showed a dead\n''No sessions found'' with no way to message a registered agent. Add an ''Agents''\npicker section (always shown, sourced from the agents store) that opens an\nagent_<name> conversation, plus a ''Conversations'' section so started direct\nchats actually appear in the list. On the server, emit the ''session offline,\nretry'' status reply for agent_<name> conversations too (not just coord:), so\nmessaging an agent with no live session gives feedback instead of silence.\n\nCloses #611.\n\n* perf(scheduler): run ANALYZE in auto_cleanup; make claude scan interval configurable\n\nRun db ANALYZE after auto_cleanup to refresh query-planner statistics, and\nmake the Claude session scan interval tunable via MC_CLAUDE_SCAN_INTERVAL_MS\n(default 60s) for large ~/.claude/projects trees.\n\nApplied from PR #709 by yojen7 (security-audited + verified clean).\n\n* perf(sessions): make session file size limit configurable via MC_MAX_SESSION_FILE_BYTES\n\nReplace the hardcoded 50MB MAX_SESSION_FILE_BYTES cap (used to skip oversized\nJSONL session files) with an env-driven value, defaulting to the existing 50MB.\n\nApplied from PR #710 by yojen7 (security-audited + verified clean).\n\n* feat(security): harden workspace-scoped route access (#668)\n\nReplace the silent `workspace_id ?? 1` fallback across task/comment/queue/\nheartbeat/memory/webhook routes with fail-closed requireWorkspaceId (400 when\nmissing/invalid), and restrict non-admin agent-scoped API keys to their own\nagent and assigned tasks via a new src/lib/enforcement/workspace-scope.ts\n(requireAgentSelfAccess / requireAgentTaskAccess). Admins and human users are\nunaffected. Ships 45 tests across 7 files.\n\nApplied from PR #668 by niko4244. Security-audited + independently re-verified:\nfail-closed, opens no new access path, all SQL parameterized, admin\nshort-circuit can''t be reached via X-Agent-Name header. Composes with the\nlocal #662 (heartbeat) and #663 (tasks) changes.\n\n* chore(security): enable 7-day supply-chain cooldown (Dependabot + pnpm)\n\nAdd .github/dependabot.yml with a 7-day cooldown for npm/github-actions/docker\nupdates, and pnpm minimumReleaseAge=10080 (7 days) so newly published versions\naren''t installed until the ecosystem has had time to detect/yank a compromised\nrelease. Defense in depth at both the update-proposal and resolve layers.\n\nReconstructed from PR #707 by cassao29 (rebased onto the current pnpm config;\ncomments translated to English).\n\n* feat(health): public /api/health + /health probe; atomic task-claim (#698)\n\nAdd unauthenticated /api/health and /health routes for upstream watchdogs\n(exact-match proxy allowlist, no wildcard). Unlike the original PR, the routes\nexpose only a coarse reachability signal — NO task_count and NO raw DB error\nmessages — to avoid info disclosure to anonymous probes. Also adopt the PR''s\natomic task-claim fix in dispatchAssignedTasks (UPDATE ... WHERE status =\n''assigned'') to prevent double-dispatch under concurrent schedulers.\n\nReconstructed from PR #698 by 7heM4ster, with two deliberate omissions: the\nDockerfile --config.dangerouslyAllowAllBuilds=true flag (a supply-chain\nhardening regression that disables the onlyBuiltDependencies allowlist) and the\nduplicate package.json onlyBuiltDependencies hunk (superseded by #702).\n\n* chore(cleanup): remove 17 orphaned UI files + unused graph deps (#680)\n\nRemove 17 dead UI components/styles with zero live importers (token-dashboard,\nsession-details, agent-cost/history panels, the old dashboard sidebar/stats/\nsessions-list/agent-network, hud/connection-status, layout/promo-banner, the\ntop-level nav-rail orphan, plugin-loader, hyperbrowser-example, design-tokens,\nagent-core-node, online-status), and drop @xyflow/react + reactflow which were\nused only by those files (reagraph stays — still used by memory-graph). Ignore\n.env.production.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, production build succeeds with full route tree intact.\n\nReconstructed from PR #680 by usamaB, with one deliberate exception: KEPT\nops/mc-provisioner-daemon.js and scripts/smoke-staging.mjs — privileged ops\ntooling with no in-repo imports that may be wired up out-of-repo (systemd/CI),\nso removing them as ''dead code'' would be unsafe.\n\n* docs: add FAQ section to README (#712)\n\nAppend an FAQ covering what MC is, key features, supported frameworks, install\nmethods, and why-choose bullets.\n\nApplied from PR #712 by meichuanyi, with one fix: replaced the hardcoded\n''577 tests'' count (already stale — the suite is now 1000+) with a\ncoverage-type description that won''t rot.\n\n* fix(pricing): correct Opus 4.5/4.6 and Haiku 4.5 token pricing (#719)\n\nUpdate Anthropic pricing to current official rates (verified 2026-05 against\nplatform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing):\n- Opus 4.5 & 4.6: 15/75 -> 5/25 per MTok (the old 15/75 is now only Opus 4.1/4)\n- Haiku 4.5: 0.8/4 -> 1/5 per MTok (Haiku 3.5 retired stays 0.8/4)\nFixes both the token-pricing.ts table and the duplicate table in\nclaude-sessions.ts (which #719 missed), and updates/extends the tests.\n\nSupersedes PR #719 by oskarkocol, which had the right direction but only\npatched 4 lines and left Opus 4.6 + the claude-sessions.ts table wrong.\n\n* test(task-dispatch): update reconciliation mock for atomic-claim SQL (#698)\n\nThe #698 atomic task-claim changed the dispatch UPDATE to\n''... WHERE id = ? AND status = ''\\''''assigned''\\'''''', which no longer matched the\nexact-string SQL branch in the reconciliation test''s getDatabase mock (so the\nclaim returned changes:0 and the task was skipped). Match both the plain and\natomic-claim SQL forms in the mock.\n\nNote: the pre-existing ''does not send heuristic model overrides'' failure in this\nfile is present on origin/main independently of this branch and is not addressed\nhere.\n\n* ci(quality-gate): drop redundant pnpm version pin (conflicts with packageManager)\n\npnpm/action-setup@v4 errors with ERR_PNPM_BAD_PM_VERSION when both a `version:`\ninput and package.json#packageManager are set. Since #702 added\npackageManager: pnpm@10.29.3 as the single source of truth, remove the\n`version: 10` from the workflow so CI resolves the same pinned version.\n\nFollow-up to #702.\n\n* docs(openapi): document GET /api/health for contract parity (#698)\n\nThe new public /api/health route (#698) failed ''pnpm api:parity'' because it\nwasn''t in openapi.json. Add its spec (Monitoring tag, security: [], 200 ok /\n503 degraded shapes) so route↔spec parity holds.\n\n* test(task-dispatch): make gateway-path tests deterministic vs isGatewayAvailable\n\nisGatewayAvailable() (rewritten in #648) requires a real openclaw.json on disk\nOR a healthy gateways row; it no longer trusts config.openclawHome alone. The\nreconciliation tests mock neither, so on hosts with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or the\nclaude CLI they fell through to the direct-API path and made a real network\ncall (failing with a credit-balance error) instead of the asserted gateway\npath. Report a healthy gateway row in the getDatabase mock so the gateway path\nis taken deterministically. Fixes a pre-existing env-dependent failure.\n\n* fix(tokens,pipelines): stop double-counting token usage; standardize DELETE body\n\nfix(tokens): a single POST /api/tokens persists the same usage to BOTH the JSON\nfile and the token_usage table, then the agent-costs/task-costs aggregation\nmerged both via dedupeTokenRecords. The dedup key keyed on raw-ms timestamp and\non operation — but the DB copy stores created_at in SECONDS (read back as *1000)\nand the DB loader hardcodes operation:''heartbeat'' (no operation column), so the\ntwo copies of one event never deduped and every posted record was counted twice.\nNormalize the timestamp to whole seconds and drop operation from the key.\n\nfix(pipelines): standardize DELETE /api/pipelines on a JSON body (Issue #18) —\nreject requests with no body (''Request body required'', 400) and stop accepting\nthe legacy ?id= query param, matching webhooks/settings/workflows/backup/auth.\n\nBoth fix pre-existing E2E failures that origin/main''s red unit suite was masking.","tree":{"sha":"1b03e37840732901ac5241c4205f76565dd72fee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/git/trees/1b03e37840732901ac5241c4205f76565dd72fee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/git/commits/6188cc492651acae78a5d8e5dac45324c69f455b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b03e37840732901ac5241c4205f76565dd72fee\nparent 85215c577f491cf570aa667e6757d8b30e201d0a\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1780209616 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780209616 +0700\n\nfix: resolve open issue/PR backlog (security audits + fixes + apiFetch migration) (#723)\n\n* fix(command): return actionable error on ENOENT spawn failure (#588)\n\nWhen a runtime binary (openclaw/clawdbot) is missing from PATH, surface a\nfriendly message naming the missing command and the *_BIN override env var\ninstead of a raw ''spawn ENOENT''.\n\n* docs: refresh README screenshots and ignore docs/_*.png debug artifacts\n\n* fix(build): pin pnpm to v10 and complete onlyBuiltDependencies allowlist (#702)\n\npnpm 11 turns ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS into a hard error, breaking fresh\nDocker builds. Pin pnpm@10.29.3 via packageManager + Dockerfile (matching\nCI) and extend onlyBuiltDependencies to cover all native deps that ship\nbuild scripts (@parcel/watcher, @swc/core, esbuild, sharp, unrs-resolver).\n\nCloses #702. Supersedes #703, #705, #713.\n\n* fix(security): handle SecretRef-form gateway auth credentials (#670)\n\n/api/security-audit crashed with ''trim is not a function'' when\ngateway.auth.token/.password is a SecretRef object (vault/file-backed)\ninstead of a plain string. Add a hasCredential() typeguard that treats any\nnon-null value as configured; the resolved value is validated by OpenClaw\nat runtime. Adds a regression test covering string, empty, missing, and\nSecretRef forms.\n\nCloses #670. Supersedes #674 (NePav).\n\n* feat(api-client): add apiFetch with global 401/403/5xx handling (#681)\n\nAdds apiFetch<T>() (src/lib/api-client.ts) that sends cookies, redirects to\n/login on 401 (with a redirect-loop guard), and throws typed ApiError for\n403/404/5xx/network/parse failures. Mounts AuthExpiredListener at the root\nlayout and adds a warn-level eslint rule discouraging bare fetch(''/api/...'').\n\nReconstructed from PR #681 authored by jun261930-tech (the original branch was\ncut from a pre-hardening base, so it is re-applied here rather than merged).\nSecurity-audited + independently re-verified: same-origin only, sameSite=strict\ncookie can''t leak cross-origin, /login ''from'' param is inert (never read).\nDropped the non-functional TemplateLiteral eslint selector.\n\n* fix(ui): stop focus trap from stealing focus on re-render (#673)\n\nuseFocusTrap bundled initial-focus with the keydown-listener effect, keyed on\nthe recreated handleKeyDown. When a parent re-rendered (e.g. on every SSE\nupdate during task editing), the effect re-ran and refocused the first field,\nyanking the cursor from the description back to the title. Split into a\nmount-only focus/restore effect ([] deps) and a separate listener effect.\n\nCloses #673.\n\n* fix(gateway): negotiate protocol range 3..4 instead of pinning v3 (#701)\n\nThe connect handshake hardcoded PROTOCOL_VERSION=3 as both minProtocol and\nmaxProtocol, so OpenClaw 2026.5.18+ (which requires maxProtocol>=4) rejected\nthe handshake with ''protocol mismatch''. Advertise a [min,max] window (3..4) via\na testable buildProtocolNegotiation() helper in websocket-utils, staying\nbackward-compatible with v3-only gateways. Adds unit tests.\n\nCloses #701.\n\n* feat(tasks): auto-route unassigned tasks to coordinator agent (#663)\n\nMC_COORDINATOR_AGENT was documented but never consumed by task creation. Add\nconfig.coordinatorAgent (opt-in; empty = disabled) and a pure resolveTaskAssignee()\nhelper, then thread the resolved assignee through the INSERT, status\nnormalization, activity log, and assignment notification in POST /api/tasks.\nNew tasks created without an assignee now route to the coordinator when set.\n\nCloses #663.\n\n* fix(heartbeat): stop returning the same mentions on every poll (#662)\n\nThe heartbeat GET built a ''mentions'' work item from a raw comments query with\nonly a 4h time filter and no read-state, so the same mentions reappeared on\nevery poll for 4 hours. Comment creation already emits acknowledgeable\n''mention''-type notifications (surfaced by the unread-notifications work item),\nmaking that query redundant. Remove it; mentions are now acknowledged by\nmarking their notification read.\n\nCloses #662.\n\n* fix(spawn): fall back to modern agent method when sessions_spawn is gone (#645)\n\nOpenClaw 2026.5.x removed the sessions_spawn gateway method, so the Spawn\nbutton failed with ''unknown method: sessions_spawn''. Detect that error via a\nnew isUnknownMethodError() helper and fall back to the modern ''agent''\ninvocation (message param) that task-dispatch already uses. Reports which\nmethod was used in the audit log + response.\n\nCloses #645.\n\n* refactor: migrate 188 bare fetch(''/api/...'') sites to apiFetch (#682-#697)\n\nMigrate 21 components/panels from bare fetch to apiFetch<T>() so 401/403/5xx/\nnetwork failures are handled uniformly (401 redirects to /login; the rest throw\ntyped ApiError). Each call site preserves its original behavior: graceful-\ndegradation sites keep their try/catch swallow, server error messages are\nre-surfaced via ApiError.payload, and redundant Content-Type headers are\ndropped. Verified: 0 bare /api fetches remain, tsc clean, 964 unit tests pass,\nno new lint warnings.\n\nReconstructed from the apiFetch migration series by jun261930-tech (PRs\nmigration was re-derived on current main per-file). Fixes a latent bug in the\noriginal chat migration where conversation-list computed but never used its\nparsed sessions.\n\n* fix(tasks): correct comment-tab count and stop scroll reset on poll (#664, #660)\n\n#664: the comments-tab badge used comments.length (top-level threads only)\nwhile the task-card badge uses a flat COUNT(*) over all comments. Add a pure\ncountCommentsDeep() that recurses through replies so both badges agree.\n\n#660: fetchComments toggled loadingComments on every 15s background poll,\nunmounting the comment list and resetting the user''s scroll position. Gate the\nloading placeholder behind a first-load ref so the DOM stays mounted across\npolls; reset the guard when switching tasks.\n\nCloses #664, #660.\n\n* fix(chat): let users start conversations with registered agents (#611)\n\nThe chat conversation list never invoked its onNewConversation prop and only\nrendered gateway/local sessions, so when no sessions existed it showed a dead\n''No sessions found'' with no way to message a registered agent. Add an ''Agents''\npicker section (always shown, sourced from the agents store) that opens an\nagent_<name> conversation, plus a ''Conversations'' section so started direct\nchats actually appear in the list. On the server, emit the ''session offline,\nretry'' status reply for agent_<name> conversations too (not just coord:), so\nmessaging an agent with no live session gives feedback instead of silence.\n\nCloses #611.\n\n* perf(scheduler): run ANALYZE in auto_cleanup; make claude scan interval configurable\n\nRun db ANALYZE after auto_cleanup to refresh query-planner statistics, and\nmake the Claude session scan interval tunable via MC_CLAUDE_SCAN_INTERVAL_MS\n(default 60s) for large ~/.claude/projects trees.\n\nApplied from PR #709 by yojen7 (security-audited + verified clean).\n\n* perf(sessions): make session file size limit configurable via MC_MAX_SESSION_FILE_BYTES\n\nReplace the hardcoded 50MB MAX_SESSION_FILE_BYTES cap (used to skip oversized\nJSONL session files) with an env-driven value, defaulting to the existing 50MB.\n\nApplied from PR #710 by yojen7 (security-audited + verified clean).\n\n* feat(security): harden workspace-scoped route access (#668)\n\nReplace the silent `workspace_id ?? 1` fallback across task/comment/queue/\nheartbeat/memory/webhook routes with fail-closed requireWorkspaceId (400 when\nmissing/invalid), and restrict non-admin agent-scoped API keys to their own\nagent and assigned tasks via a new src/lib/enforcement/workspace-scope.ts\n(requireAgentSelfAccess / requireAgentTaskAccess). Admins and human users are\nunaffected. Ships 45 tests across 7 files.\n\nApplied from PR #668 by niko4244. Security-audited + independently re-verified:\nfail-closed, opens no new access path, all SQL parameterized, admin\nshort-circuit can''t be reached via X-Agent-Name header. Composes with the\nlocal #662 (heartbeat) and #663 (tasks) changes.\n\n* chore(security): enable 7-day supply-chain cooldown (Dependabot + pnpm)\n\nAdd .github/dependabot.yml with a 7-day cooldown for npm/github-actions/docker\nupdates, and pnpm minimumReleaseAge=10080 (7 days) so newly published versions\naren''t installed until the ecosystem has had time to detect/yank a compromised\nrelease. Defense in depth at both the update-proposal and resolve layers.\n\nReconstructed from PR #707 by cassao29 (rebased onto the current pnpm config;\ncomments translated to English).\n\n* feat(health): public /api/health + /health probe; atomic task-claim (#698)\n\nAdd unauthenticated /api/health and /health routes for upstream watchdogs\n(exact-match proxy allowlist, no wildcard). Unlike the original PR, the routes\nexpose only a coarse reachability signal — NO task_count and NO raw DB error\nmessages — to avoid info disclosure to anonymous probes. Also adopt the PR''s\natomic task-claim fix in dispatchAssignedTasks (UPDATE ... WHERE status =\n''assigned'') to prevent double-dispatch under concurrent schedulers.\n\nReconstructed from PR #698 by 7heM4ster, with two deliberate omissions: the\nDockerfile --config.dangerouslyAllowAllBuilds=true flag (a supply-chain\nhardening regression that disables the onlyBuiltDependencies allowlist) and the\nduplicate package.json onlyBuiltDependencies hunk (superseded by #702).\n\n* chore(cleanup): remove 17 orphaned UI files + unused graph deps (#680)\n\nRemove 17 dead UI components/styles with zero live importers (token-dashboard,\nsession-details, agent-cost/history panels, the old dashboard sidebar/stats/\nsessions-list/agent-network, hud/connection-status, layout/promo-banner, the\ntop-level nav-rail orphan, plugin-loader, hyperbrowser-example, design-tokens,\nagent-core-node, online-status), and drop @xyflow/react + reactflow which were\nused only by those files (reagraph stays — still used by memory-graph). Ignore\n.env.production.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, production build succeeds with full route tree intact.\n\nReconstructed from PR #680 by usamaB, with one deliberate exception: KEPT\nops/mc-provisioner-daemon.js and scripts/smoke-staging.mjs — privileged ops\ntooling with no in-repo imports that may be wired up out-of-repo (systemd/CI),\nso removing them as ''dead code'' would be unsafe.\n\n* docs: add FAQ section to README (#712)\n\nAppend an FAQ covering what MC is, key features, supported frameworks, install\nmethods, and why-choose bullets.\n\nApplied from PR #712 by meichuanyi, with one fix: replaced the hardcoded\n''577 tests'' count (already stale — the suite is now 1000+) with a\ncoverage-type description that won''t rot.\n\n* fix(pricing): correct Opus 4.5/4.6 and Haiku 4.5 token pricing (#719)\n\nUpdate Anthropic pricing to current official rates (verified 2026-05 against\nplatform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing):\n- Opus 4.5 & 4.6: 15/75 -> 5/25 per MTok (the old 15/75 is now only Opus 4.1/4)\n- Haiku 4.5: 0.8/4 -> 1/5 per MTok (Haiku 3.5 retired stays 0.8/4)\nFixes both the token-pricing.ts table and the duplicate table in\nclaude-sessions.ts (which #719 missed), and updates/extends the tests.\n\nSupersedes PR #719 by oskarkocol, which had the right direction but only\npatched 4 lines and left Opus 4.6 + the claude-sessions.ts table wrong.\n\n* test(task-dispatch): update reconciliation mock for atomic-claim SQL (#698)\n\nThe #698 atomic task-claim changed the dispatch UPDATE to\n''... WHERE id = ? AND status = ''\\''''assigned''\\'''''', which no longer matched the\nexact-string SQL branch in the reconciliation test''s getDatabase mock (so the\nclaim returned changes:0 and the task was skipped). Match both the plain and\natomic-claim SQL forms in the mock.\n\nNote: the pre-existing ''does not send heuristic model overrides'' failure in this\nfile is present on origin/main independently of this branch and is not addressed\nhere.\n\n* ci(quality-gate): drop redundant pnpm version pin (conflicts with packageManager)\n\npnpm/action-setup@v4 errors with ERR_PNPM_BAD_PM_VERSION when both a `version:`\ninput and package.json#packageManager are set. Since #702 added\npackageManager: pnpm@10.29.3 as the single source of truth, remove the\n`version: 10` from the workflow so CI resolves the same pinned version.\n\nFollow-up to #702.\n\n* docs(openapi): document GET /api/health for contract parity (#698)\n\nThe new public /api/health route (#698) failed ''pnpm api:parity'' because it\nwasn''t in openapi.json. Add its spec (Monitoring tag, security: [], 200 ok /\n503 degraded shapes) so route↔spec parity holds.\n\n* test(task-dispatch): make gateway-path tests deterministic vs isGatewayAvailable\n\nisGatewayAvailable() (rewritten in #648) requires a real openclaw.json on disk\nOR a healthy gateways row; it no longer trusts config.openclawHome alone. The\nreconciliation tests mock neither, so on hosts with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or the\nclaude CLI they fell through to the direct-API path and made a real network\ncall (failing with a credit-balance error) instead of the asserted gateway\npath. Report a healthy gateway row in the getDatabase mock so the gateway path\nis taken deterministically. Fixes a pre-existing env-dependent failure.\n\n* fix(tokens,pipelines): stop double-counting token usage; standardize DELETE body\n\nfix(tokens): a single POST /api/tokens persists the same usage to BOTH the JSON\nfile and the token_usage table, then the agent-costs/task-costs aggregation\nmerged both via dedupeTokenRecords. The dedup key keyed on raw-ms timestamp and\non operation — but the DB copy stores created_at in SECONDS (read back as *1000)\nand the DB loader hardcodes operation:''heartbeat'' (no operation column), so the\ntwo copies of one event never deduped and every posted record was counted twice.\nNormalize the timestamp to whole seconds and drop operation from the key.\n\nfix(pipelines): standardize DELETE /api/pipelines on a JSON body (Issue #18) —\nreject requests with no body (''Request body required'', 400) and stop accepting\nthe legacy ?id= query param, matching webhooks/settings/workflows/backup/auth.\n\nBoth fix pre-existing E2E failures that origin/main''s red unit suite was masking.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqG9fRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgDoQAKtlJs2H8b/8657KAlEVQsJK\nAnI7Bg/PJF8axtF9IMrAmbk7Yy1LdK0ErihfCQkYVDtuOnlAJia7RCIe5uccmpye\nGE5WwsqaBytMTBnn+fiHpSjZAXoJK3+wKplCvOxn4VC3SnN9wfRynQNAzCjxGOob\nypB9BVWGQrHvZ4nLdnkeVe+/+LkB8EdnJqTomnoqZ2urBenbIx5N6ySO5rBzGrWp\n/yERFc/t+sw3eCFvNSUUmEdvFxWj1WYnFmkYAKw+kFJ1bUJ88sLTWilW49f8edy1\nr2ovJ/n1KO44Fk9GgfCDNQj0J9fryiiwYRRKZU6c9Cn8U4g57JcyK6MlEOzfDKB2\nJrEUKizGxbUp9RE4AkDQSVptsOkBtZHZze08cg2ump2qU94067aUEAEG1hA373RY\nhupiyDGlL5KpFerqLrtTVKUvlhoBL7j/5Y9Z9ZVJiUuqawQaR8KQ7S9CpnIQDbh8\nRNQk2+NiEaeD1SurZKbLt6onDhX9hefIt/PcKzEpRxpUSAhCzbB1Gh9kL0DoJYGj\nbk8FV2MNXQamH8LZVLkQx+k3JPStg99q7AK0jx3JRHadXEmf++3BhY/EqysS4zsE\nlsfLYzz8HGKgczNoU+2hadE/Y5WYoCGLnPolY7HeSaF0s/coHnEHdvVbAjLW+CFG\nntAodthlZuKPOrdiSaZD\n=9PM/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-31T06:40:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api