s-martin-locki","id":258319624,"login":"lucas-martin-locki","node_id":"U_kgDOD2WlCA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucas-martin-locki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucas-martin-locki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucas-martin-locki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucas-martin-locki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucas-martin-locki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucas-martin-locki","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jonochocki/mission-control/commit/d29febac384bbd418f3bc957730fba9179743bdf","node_id":"C_kwDOSsbBo9oAKGQyOWZlYmFjMzg0YmJkNDE4ZjNiYzk1NzczMGZiYTkxNzk3NDNiZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jonochocki/mission-control/commit/8517d5e89694e4ab1b65f4b6c1e206ec1b632288","sha":"8517d5e89694e4ab1b65f4b6c1e206ec1b632288","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/commits/8517d5e89694e4ab1b65f4b6c1e206ec1b632288"}],"sha":"d29febac384bbd418f3bc957730fba9179743bdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/commits/d29febac384bbd418f3bc957730fba9179743bdf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/commits/85215c577f491cf570aa667e6757d8b30e201d0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:59:40Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:59:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(recurring-tasks): include HH:MM in child title for sub-daily crons (#659)\n\nCloses #616.\n\nProblem\n-------\n\nRecurring tasks with sub-daily cron schedules (e.g. `0 * * * *` hourly,\n`*/5 * * * *` every-5-min) only spawned once per calendar day. All\nsubsequent spawns within the same day were silently skipped.\n\nRoot cause: `spawnRecurringTasks` derives child titles from\n`formatDateSuffix()` which only emitted day-level granularity (`MMM DD`).\nThe duplicate-prevention guard at recurring-tasks.ts:75-79 then matches\non `(title, workspace_id, project_id)` and finds the previous spawn,\nreturning early.\n\nFix\n---\n\n  1. New `isSubDailyCron(cronExpr)` helper returns true when the\n     minute or hour field is anything other than a single concrete\n     number (covers wildcards, ranges, lists, steps).\n\n  2. `formatDateSuffix(now, subDaily)` now takes an explicit `now`\n     and a `subDaily` flag:\n\n        Daily / weekly / monthly:  \"Apr 24\"           (unchanged)\n        Sub-daily:                 \"Apr 24, 13:35\"\n\n     Same-day spawns at 13:00 and 14:00 now produce different titles\n     and the duplicate-guard correctly admits both.\n\n  3. Daily/weekly/monthly title format is preserved so existing\n     operator workflows don''t see a title-churn migration.\n\nCompatibility\n-------------\n\n  - `isCronDue()` already prevents same-minute double-spawns via the\n    `lastSpawnedAtMs` check, so this PR doesn''t loosen the dedup —\n    it just stops the dedup from firing on the *wrong* layer.\n\n  - The `formatDateSuffix` signature now takes optional arguments\n    with sane defaults; existing call sites still work.\n\nTests\n-----\n\n13 new tests in src/lib/__tests__/recurring-tasks.test.ts:\n\n  - `isSubDailyCron` recognizes hourly / every-5-min / every-minute /\n    ranged-minute crons; rejects daily/weekly; defensive on malformed.\n  - `formatDateSuffix` returns `MMM DD` (daily) and `MMM DD, HH:MM`\n    (sub-daily); zero-pads day-of-month.\n  - Regression: two hourly spawns on the same day produce different titles.\n  - Regression: every-5-min spawns within the same hour produce different titles.\n  - Daily cron preserves historical \"MMM DD\" shape.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"635aefae71845767a0277a3160a1260b9bd76776","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/git/trees/635aefae71845767a0277a3160a1260b9bd76776"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonochocki/mission-control/git/commits/85215c577f491cf570aa667e6757d8b30e201d0a","verification":{"payload":"tree 635aefae71845767a0277a3160a1260b9bd76776\nparent 0f0ec68976c3662d3279821c1ed701209e4d85f0\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1778129980 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778129980 +0700\n\nfix(recurring-tasks): include HH:MM in child title for sub-daily crons (#659)\n\nCloses #616.\n\nProblem\n-------\n\nRecurring tasks with sub-daily cron schedules (e.g. `0 * * * *` hourly,\n`*/5 * * * *` every-5-min) only spawned once per calendar day. All\nsubsequent spawns within the same day were silently skipped.\n\nRoot cause: `spawnRecurringTasks` derives child titles from\n`formatDateSuffix()` which only emitted day-level granularity (`MMM DD`).\nThe duplicate-prevention guard at recurring-tasks.ts:75-79 then matches\non `(title, workspace_id, project_id)` and finds the previous spawn,\nreturning early.\n\nFix\n---\n\n  1. New `isSubDailyCron(cronExpr)` helper returns true when the\n     minute or hour field is anything other than a single concrete\n     number (covers wildcards, ranges, lists, steps).\n\n  2. `formatDateSuffix(now, subDaily)` now takes an explicit `now`\n     and a `subDaily` flag:\n\n        Daily / weekly / monthly:  \"Apr 24\"           (unchanged)\n        Sub-daily:                 \"Apr 24, 13:35\"\n\n     Same-day spawns at 13:00 and 14:00 now produce different titles\n     and the duplicate-guard correctly admits both.\n\n  3. Daily/weekly/monthly title format is preserved so existing\n     operator workflows don''t see a title-churn migration.\n\nCompatibility\n-------------\n\n  - `isCronDue()` already prevents same-minute double-spawns via the\n    `lastSpawnedAtMs` check, so this PR doesn''t loosen the dedup —\n    it just stops the dedup from firing on the *wrong* layer.\n\n  - The `formatDateSuffix` signature now takes optional arguments\n    with sane defaults; existing call sites still work.\n\nTests\n-----\n\n13 new tests in src/lib/__tests__/recurring-tasks.test.ts:\n\n  - `isSubDailyCron` recognizes hourly / every-5-min / every-minute /\n    ranged-minute crons; rejects daily/weekly; defensive on malformed.\n  - `formatDateSuffix` returns `MMM DD` (daily) and `MMM DD, HH:MM`\n    (sub-daily); zero-pads day-of-month.\n  - Regression: two hourly spawns on the same day produce different titles.\n  - Regression: every-5-min spawns within the same hour produce different titles.\n  - Daily cron preserves historical \"MMM DD\" shape.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/Bw8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmAAQAHRkazx8b1OkBlF1VNo3/jDS\nOgJHGuXEeMi3KTrH2wMJ3sYjA3jyoxQYC5IhLBqMT1d8earjowsBbilFRmXnP66n\nID4nCwfUS9S+LSgvQRMMBNrZp8tvjz0Mnr1GG5DBtOIAc6UqEe/sj/8yC0nO2IBC\nTHuMH1hSQ0R5EeLAudYs1PkFpNfr2C+kCKhDyYO6+v1QPZI1Z2w/fDTN8VZurRS3\n7d8fhmsiQRIpbl1LebmBDYE2oF27Tupc7Jn4klTbmjPAjqJDgrAAuCUMi8QYayAf\nwEJtSh3l/zZTnGbqOxlZHjbneY/ttOm4g2sxW/AsP5R3kbjjbIxJI6Xjrs