ps://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ErickGS28/ALETHEIA/commits/422a0494155ced29b2388f00fd54a0b9d4957371/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:27:51Z","email":"isaac777jb@gmail.com","name":"Isaac Jimenez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:27:51Z","email":"isaac777jb@gmail.com","name":"Isaac Jimenez"},"message":"fix(alexa): resolve bare month names to the current year, not next year\n\nAMAZON.DATE resolves a bare month name (\"agosto\", no year) to whichever\nyear''s occurrence comes next chronologically. If today falls inside that\nmonth, it can jump to next year instead of returning the current one\n(e.g. asking on 2026-08-06 resolved \"agosto\" to 2027-08). Now prefer the\ncurrent year''s occurrence whenever it hasn''t finished yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3036e4d9229470803e2db85b0570f9cc8517c913","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ErickGS28/ALETHEIA/git/trees/3036e4d9229470803e2db85b0570f9cc8517c913"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ErickGS28/ALETHEIA/git/commits/422a0494155ced29b2388f00fd54a0b9d4957371","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/120062171?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isaacjbar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"htt