1d5","node_id":"C_kwDOSuYchdoAKDg4YjQ1NWY4OGNmMWI4ZTU2YmNiY2RiODBmZjIxODA4ZWEwZWYxZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Obryko/monorepo-template/commit/6e3b3f74b46700d163d54c9f32396d242db1ac3e","sha":"6e3b3f74b46700d163d54c9f32396d242db1ac3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/commits/6e3b3f74b46700d163d54c9f32396d242db1ac3e"}],"sha":"88b455f88cf1b8e56bcbcdb80ff21808ea0ef1d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/commits/88b455f88cf1b8e56bcbcdb80ff21808ea0ef1d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20777657?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Obryko","id":20777657,"login":"Obryko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzc3NjU3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/commits/6e3b3f74b46700d163d54c9f32396d242db1ac3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T17:42:55Z","email":"kacperobrycki@gmail.com","name":"Kacper Obrycki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T17:42:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add apps/remote MF remote app and wire to shell (#6)\n\n* chore: commit missing packages (contracts, typescript-config, linter, env files)\n\n* feat(web): migrate from Vite to Rsbuild with Module Federation host\n\n- Replace vite.config.ts with rsbuild.config.ts using @rsbuild/core\n- Register apps/web as MF shell host via pluginModuleFederation\n  (remotes: {} — no active remotes yet; React/ReactDOM as eager singletons)\n- Replace @tailwindcss/vite with @tailwindcss/postcss via Rsbuild PostCSS\n- Replace @vitejs/plugin-react with @rsbuild/plugin-react (SWC-based)\n- Replace @rolldown/plugin-babel with @rsbuild/plugin-babel for React Compiler\n  (no SWC Wasm plugin for React Compiler exists on npm; Babel is the documented path)\n- Add @rsbuild/core/types to tsconfig to replace vite/client types\n- Update .gitignore: .vinxi/.tanstack → .rsbuild\n- Vitest and Playwright unchanged\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add apps/remote MF remote app and wire to shell\n\n- apps/remote exposes HelloRemote component via Module Federation on port 3001\n- apps/web shell adds remote to remotes config (localhost:3001/remoteEntry.js)\n- Home route lazy-loads HelloRemote via React.lazy + Suspense (in src/components/HelloRemote.tsx)\n- Fix MF plugin environment mismatch: TanStack Start uses ''client''+''ssr'' envs, not Rsbuild''s\n  default ''web''; pass { environment: ''client'' } to pluginModuleFederation\n- Externalize remote/HelloRemote in SSR env so rspack doesn''t fail to bundle it server-side;\n  React.lazy + Suspense renders the fallback during SSR, so the external is never required\n- Add TypeScript declaration for remote/HelloRemote module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review and CI failures\n\n- HelloRemote: catch dynamic import failure and render local fallback so\n  the page does not error when the remote is down (Suspense alone cannot\n  recover from a rejected import promise)\n- apps/remote: add check, check:fix, typecheck scripts so the new\n  workspace is verified by root `pnpm typecheck` / `pnpm check`\n- Apply biome auto-fixes (organizeImports, formatting) across rsbuild\n  configs and remote.d.ts to clear Lint CI failure\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit review feedback\n\n- Env-drive remote URL via REMOTE_URL (was hardcoded localhost:3001)\n- Remove duplicate port from apps/remote rsbuild config (CLI flag wins)\n- Add bootstrap entry point for apps/remote standalone dev/preview\n- Add HelloRemote.displayName for React DevTools\n- Align build:remote filter with dev:remote (drop unnecessary ... suffix)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback on rstest-mf-remote-app\n\n- HelloRemote: log dynamic import error in dev before rendering fallback\n- apps/remote: consolidate dev port into rsbuild.config.ts (server.port: 3001)\n- apps/remote: add biome.json (root: false, extends: //)\n- apps/web/.gitignore: ignore .tanstack/ temp dir\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web): drop eager: true from MF shared deps to fix dev async chunks\n\nWith `shared: { react: { eager: true } }` on the MF host config, rspack''s\nchunk loader rejects TanStack Router''s auto-split async chunks at hydration\n(\"Loading chunk src_routes_index_tsx_tsr-split_component failed\"). The chunk\nfile is served (HTTP 200) but the MF runtime treats it as invalid because\neager singletons collide with the dynamically-loaded route module.\n\nRemoving `eager: true` lets the chunk register normally. The host still\nshares React/ReactDOM as singletons with the remote — eager loading isn''t\nrequired for that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review and CI feedback\n\n- move remote dev server to port 3002 to avoid API conflict (3001)\n- update REMOTE_URL default in .env.example and web rsbuild config\n- drop swallowing .catch in HelloRemote (caused hydration mismatch risk\n  and cached failure in React.lazy)\n- add ... closure to build:remote filter to match build:api/build:web\n- regenerate lockfile after merging main\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review — add RemoteErrorBoundary for graceful offline\n\nWrap <HelloRemote/> with RemoteErrorBoundary at the route level so the\npage degrades to a small fallback when the MF remote is unavailable,\nwithout re-introducing the .catch() that swallowed lazy errors and\ncaused hydration/cache issues.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: exclude generated *.gen.ts from Sonar analysis\n\nrouteTree.gen.ts is emitted by the TanStack Router generator with a\nblanket /* eslint-disable */, which Sonar flags. The file is not\nauthored, so exclude all *.gen.ts from analysis instead of trying to\nedit generator output.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review — gate remote to client + drop eslint header\n\n- Wrap <HelloRemote/> in <ClientOnly fallback={...}> so SSR renders the\n  same Loading fallback markup and never starts the dynamic MF import\n  server-side, eliminating runtime risk from the externalized specifier.\n- Configure tanstackStart router.routeTreeFileHeader to drop the default\n  ''/* eslint-disable */'' line (repo uses Biome, not ESLint). Re-emit\n  routeTree.gen.ts without it via pnpm build:web.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcb62b1162be1a9434219feaac80cbf37e197ae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/git/trees/dcb62b1162be1a9434219feaac80cbf37e197ae8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/git/commits/6e3b3f74b46700d163d54c9f32396d242db1ac3e","verification":{"payload":"tree dcb62b1162be1a9434219feaac80cbf37e197ae8\nparent 8de751ac0c774716e1ea20d1794ea40dc550952c\nauthor Kacper Obrycki <kacperobrycki@gmail.com> 1780681375 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780681375 +0000\n\nfeat: add apps/remote MF remote app and wire to shell (#6)\n\n* chore: commit missing packages (contracts, typescript-config, linter, env files)\n\n* feat(web): migrate from Vite to Rsbuild with Module Federation host\n\n- Replace vite.config.ts with rsbuild.config.ts using @rsbuild/core\n- Register apps/web as MF shell host via pluginModuleFederation\n  (remotes: {} — no active remotes yet; React/ReactDOM as eager singletons)\n- Replace @tailwindcss/vite with @tailwindcss/postcss via Rsbuild PostCSS\n- Replace @vitejs/plugin-react with @rsbuild/plugin-react (SWC-based)\n- Replace @rolldown/plugin-babel with @rsbuild/plugin-babel for React Compiler\n  (no SWC Wasm plugin for React Compiler exists on npm; Babel is the documented path)\n- Add @rsbuild/core/types to tsconfig to replace vite/client types\n- Update .gitignore: .vinxi/.tanstack → .rsbuild\n- Vitest and Playwright unchanged\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add apps/remote MF remote app and wire to shell\n\n- apps/remote exposes HelloRemote component via Module Federation on port 3001\n- apps/web shell adds remote to remotes config (localhost:3001/remoteEntry.js)\n- Home route lazy-loads HelloRemote via React.lazy + Suspense (in src/components/HelloRemote.tsx)\n- Fix MF plugin environment mismatch: TanStack Start uses ''client''+''ssr'' envs, not Rsbuild''s\n  default ''web''; pass { environment: ''client'' } to pluginModuleFederation\n- Externalize remote/HelloRemote in SSR env so rspack doesn''t fail to bundle it server-side;\n  React.lazy + Suspense renders the fallback during SSR, so the external is never required\n- Add TypeScript declaration for remote/HelloRemote module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review and CI failures\n\n- HelloRemote: catch dynamic import failure and render local fallback so\n  the page does not error when the remote is down (Suspense alone cannot\n  recover from a rejected import promise)\n- apps/remote: add check, check:fix, typecheck scripts so the new\n  workspace is verified by root `pnpm typecheck` / `pnpm check`\n- Apply biome auto-fixes (organizeImports, formatting) across rsbuild\n  configs and remote.d.ts to clear Lint CI failure\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit review feedback\n\n- Env-drive remote URL via REMOTE_URL (was hardcoded localhost:3001)\n- Remove duplicate port from apps/remote rsbuild config (CLI flag wins)\n- Add bootstrap entry point for apps/remote standalone dev/preview\n- Add HelloRemote.displayName for React DevTools\n- Align build:remote filter with dev:remote (drop unnecessary ... suffix)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback on rstest-mf-remote-app\n\n- HelloRemote: log dynamic import error in dev before rendering fallback\n- apps/remote: consolidate dev port into rsbuild.config.ts (server.port: 3001)\n- apps/remote: add biome.json (root: false, extends: //)\n- apps/web/.gitignore: ignore .tanstack/ temp dir\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web): drop eager: true from MF shared deps to fix dev async chunks\n\nWith `shared: { react: { eager: true } }` on the MF host config, rspack''s\nchunk loader rejects TanStack Router''s auto-split async chunks at hydration\n(\"Loading chunk src_routes_index_tsx_tsr-split_component failed\"). The chunk\nfile is served (HTTP 200) but the MF runtime treats it as invalid because\neager singletons collide with the dynamically-loaded route module.\n\nRemoving `eager: true` lets the chunk register normally. The host still\nshares React/ReactDOM as singletons with the remote — eager loading isn''t\nrequired for that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review and CI feedback\n\n- move remote dev server to port 3002 to avoid API conflict (3001)\n- update REMOTE_URL default in .env.example and web rsbuild config\n- drop swallowing .catch in HelloRemote (caused hydration mismatch risk\n  and cached failure in React.lazy)\n- add ... closure to build:remote filter to match build:api/build:web\n- regenerate lockfile after merging main\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review — add RemoteErrorBoundary for graceful offline\n\nWrap <HelloRemote/> with RemoteErrorBoundary at the route level so the\npage degrades to a small fallback when the MF remote is unavailable,\nwithout re-introducing the .catch() that swallowed lazy errors and\ncaused hydration/cache issues.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: exclude generated *.gen.ts from Sonar analysis\n\nrouteTree.gen.ts is emitted by the TanStack Router generator with a\nblanket /* eslint-disable */, which Sonar flags. The file is not\nauthored, so exclude all *.gen.ts from analysis instead of trying to\nedit generator output.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review — gate remote to client + drop eslint header\n\n- Wrap <HelloRemote/> in <ClientOnly fallback={...}> so SSR renders the\n  same Loading fallback markup and never starts the dynamic MF import\n  server-side, eliminating runtime risk from the externalized specifier.\n- Configure tanstackStart router.routeTreeFileHeader to drop the default\n  ''/* eslint-disable */'' line (repo uses Biome, not ESLint). Re-emit\n  routeTree.gen.ts without it via pnpm build:web.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIwqfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJTgQAKJodK7BVt7DX45U6jTn2W0H\nnW6rjfGvTzYv5Ab+olSLzg2tBqWUTFN5j3rs8rZanlzE0z45XhW2pCIpHDlA0+Y+\nBpmI09znM3ezthMADhNlTkJtRyW0FwzBTeh84S6MZi1X3fm5QWpkRovlqQ1SJDRb\nseVMY7oIRUkfRnvOgRBy+Sv265jqIOHPWYTxyjZsHszbsv5cJwcoFt8gr7hhV2St\nQtfcosgdasKndFhRe0RnZRpxHd/lmclYDTj+1fdBF