://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Obryko/monorepo-template/commit/dfcf68c1ce852c155e9b75970f16abc376addf1a","node_id":"C_kwDOSuYchdoAKGRmY2Y2OGMxY2U4NTJjMTU1ZTliNzU5NzBmMTZhYmMzNzZhZGRmMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Obryko/monorepo-template/commit/4014d85f5e8bede16bb0678e81cd7f1fed55b84a","sha":"4014d85f5e8bede16bb0678e81cd7f1fed55b84a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/commits/4014d85f5e8bede16bb0678e81cd7f1fed55b84a"}],"sha":"dfcf68c1ce852c155e9b75970f16abc376addf1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/commits/dfcf68c1ce852c155e9b75970f16abc376addf1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20777657?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Obryko","id":20777657,"login":"Obryko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzc3NjU3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obryko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/commits/4014d85f5e8bede16bb0678e81cd7f1fed55b84a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T08:55:08Z","email":"kacperobrycki@gmail.com","name":"Kacper Obrycki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T08:55:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(test): migrate node packages from Vitest to Rstest (#21)\n\n* chore: commit missing packages (contracts, typescript-config, linter, env files)\n\n* chore: add Mergify, CodeRabbit, and SonarCloud configs\n\n- .mergify.yml: auto-merge Dependabot PRs on CI pass, merge queue for labelled PRs\n- .coderabbit.yaml: AI review with path-specific instructions for API, web, db, ui\n- sonar-project.properties: SonarCloud project config (fill in YOUR_GITHUB_ORG)\n- ci.yml: SonarCloud job gated behind SONAR_ENABLED repo variable to opt-in\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review and CI lint failures\n\n- Apply Biome formatter across package.json, tsconfig.json, biome.json, and source files\n- Enable tailwindDirectives in shared CSS parser config so @source compiles in web\n- Add typescript devDependency to @monorepo-template/contracts (uses tsc directly via typecheck and Vitest typecheck.checker)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use relative path in biome extends\n\nCI biome failed to resolve @monorepo-template/linter/biome via the package''s\nexports map (124 format errors against 2-space indent because the shared\nindentStyle config was never loaded). Reference the file directly so the path\nresolution does not depend on biome''s npm package lookup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: commit untracked root files\n\nbiome''s vcs.useIgnoreFile=true requires .gitignore present, otherwise the\nformatter aborts. Commit the rest of the untracked template-essential files in\nthe same change so a fresh clone matches what''s been running locally:\n\n- .gitignore, .dockerignore\n- .github/dependabot.yml, .github/copilot-instructions.md\n- .husky/pre-commit, .husky/pre-push\n- CLAUDE.md, README.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-e2e): invoke vite directly so --host actually binds 127.0.0.1\n\nThe previous webServer command was \\`pnpm dev -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port N\\`.\npnpm forwards args after \\`--\\` to the script, but the script already had its\nown \\`--port 3000\\` flag, so vite ran as\n\\`vite dev --port 3000 -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port N\\`, treating the second set\nas positional args and ignoring them. Vite bound to its default localhost\n(IPv6 on Linux CI) while Playwright probed 127.0.0.1 (IPv4-only), so the\nwebServer poll timed out at 120s. Calling vite directly via \\`pnpm exec\\`\napplies the host/port flags as intended.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback\n\n- ci(sonar): pin actions to SHAs, add persist-credentials: false, switch\n  to maintained SonarSource/sonarqube-scan-action (sonarcloud-github-action archived)\n- mergify: gate merge queue + dependabot auto-merge on API E2E and Web E2E\n- sonar: drop tsconfigPath (no root tsconfig); switch lcov.reportPaths to\n  per-workspace glob (apps/*/coverage/lcov.info, packages/*/coverage/lcov.info)\n- env: add unit tests for loadExistingEnvFiles (loads existing files, skips\n  missing, earlier files win since loadEnvFile does not overwrite)\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback (Husky, biome, coverage, docs portability)\n\n- .husky/pre-commit: chain lint-staged && precommit:typecheck so lint failures block commits\n- biome.json: extend @monorepo-template/linter/biome (package ref) instead of relative path\n- packages/contracts/vitest.config.ts: set globals: false to match other workspaces\n- packages/contracts/tsconfig.test.json: drop vitest/globals types (consistency)\n- .dockerignore: add **/.env and **/.env.* (block nested env files from build context)\n- README.md, CLAUDE.md: switch sed -i to perl -i for cross-platform portability\n- Add @vitest/coverage-v8 to catalog and to every workspace running vitest\n- Add per-workspace test:coverage scripts emitting lcov for SonarCloud\n- Root test:coverage script; CI sonar job now calls it instead of broken `pnpm test --coverage`\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: add language specifier to README code fence\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address remaining PR review feedback\n\n- add sh shebang to husky hooks (forward-compat with Husky 10)\n- document sonar-project.properties placeholder replacement in template rename steps\n- fix MD022/MD031 blank lines around CLAUDE.md headings and code fences\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): set SONAR_HOST_URL and use tag pins for sonar job\n\n- SONAR_HOST_URL set to sonarcloud.io so sonarqube-scan-action targets the right host\n- replace SHA pins on sonar job actions with version tags to match the rest of the workflow\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(test): migrate node packages from Vitest to Rstest\n\nReplace Vitest with @rstest/core in contracts, db, env, and observability\npackages. Add @rstest/core to pnpm catalog. Drop test:coverage scripts\n(Rstest coverage support pending). Update all test file imports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"20b3288149f5293db1e5c30bfd6f9e01485acd4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/git/trees/20b3288149f5293db1e5c30bfd6f9e01485acd4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obryko/monorepo-template/git/commits/4014d85f5e8bede16bb0678e81cd7f1fed55b84a","verification":{"payload":"tree 20b3288149f5293db1e5c30bfd6f9e01485acd4c\nparent e9493ee73a2ecb312bafca4ee16e1af3a6dde166\nauthor Kacper Obrycki <kacperobrycki@gmail.com> 1780649708 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780649708 +0000\n\nfeat(test): migrate node packages from Vitest to Rstest (#21)\n\n* chore: commit missing packages (contracts, typescript-config, linter, env files)\n\n* chore: add Mergify, CodeRabbit, and SonarCloud configs\n\n- .mergify.yml: auto-merge Dependabot PRs on CI pass, merge queue for labelled PRs\n- .coderabbit.yaml: AI review with path-specific instructions for API, web, db, ui\n- sonar-project.properties: SonarCloud project config (fill in YOUR_GITHUB_ORG)\n- ci.yml: SonarCloud job gated behind SONAR_ENABLED repo variable to opt-in\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review and CI lint failures\n\n- Apply Biome formatter across package.json, tsconfig.json, biome.json, and source files\n- Enable tailwindDirectives in shared CSS parser config so @source compiles in web\n- Add typescript devDependency to @monorepo-template/contracts (uses tsc directly via typecheck and Vitest typecheck.checker)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use relative path in biome extends\n\nCI biome failed to resolve @monorepo-template/linter/biome via the package''s\nexports map (124 format errors against 2-space indent because the shared\nindentStyle config was never loaded). Reference the file directly so the path\nresolution does not depend on biome''s npm package lookup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: commit untracked root files\n\nbiome''s vcs.useIgnoreFile=true requires .gitignore present, otherwise the\nformatter aborts. Commit the rest of the untracked template-essential files in\nthe same change so a fresh clone matches what''s been running locally:\n\n- .gitignore, .dockerignore\n- .github/dependabot.yml, .github/copilot-instructions.md\n- .husky/pre-commit, .husky/pre-push\n- CLAUDE.md, README.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-e2e): invoke vite directly so --host actually binds 127.0.0.1\n\nThe previous webServer command was \\`pnpm dev -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port N\\`.\npnpm forwards args after \\`--\\` to the script, but the script already had its\nown \\`--port 3000\\` flag, so vite ran as\n\\`vite dev --port 3000 -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port N\\`, treating the second set\nas positional args and ignoring them. Vite bound to its default localhost\n(IPv6 on Linux CI) while Playwright probed 127.0.0.1 (IPv4-only), so the\nwebServer poll timed out at 120s. Calling vite directly via \\`pnpm exec\\`\napplies the host/port flags as intended.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback\n\n- ci(sonar): pin actions to SHAs, add persist-credentials: false, switch\n  to maintained SonarSource/sonarqube-scan-action (sonarcloud-github-action archived)\n- mergify: gate merge queue + dependabot auto-merge on API E2E and Web E2E\n- sonar: drop tsconfigPath (no root tsconfig); switch lcov.reportPaths to\n  per-workspace glob (apps/*/coverage/lcov.info, packages/*/coverage/lcov.info)\n- env: add unit tests for loadExistingEnvFiles (loads existing files, skips\n  missing, earlier files win since loadEnvFile does not overwrite)\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback (Husky, biome, coverage, docs portability)\n\n- .husky/pre-commit: chain lint-staged && precommit:typecheck so lint failures block commits\n- biome.json: extend @monorepo-template/linter/biome (package ref) instead of relative path\n- packages/contracts/vitest.config.ts: set globals: false to match other workspaces\n- packages/contracts/tsconfig.test.json: drop vitest/globals types (consistency)\n- .dockerignore: add **/.env and **/.env.* (block nested env files from build context)\n- README.md, CLAUDE.md: switch sed -i to perl -i for cross-platform portability\n- Add @vitest/coverage-v8 to catalog and to every workspace running vitest\n- Add per-workspace test:coverage scripts emitting lcov for SonarCloud\n- Root test:coverage script; CI sonar job now calls it instead of broken `pnpm test --coverage`\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: add language specifier to README code fence\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address remaining PR review feedback\n\n- add sh shebang to husky hooks (forward-compat with Husky 10)\n- document sonar-project.properties placeholder replacement in template rename steps\n- fix MD022/MD031 blank lines around CLAUDE.md headings and code fences\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): set SONAR_HOST_URL and use tag pins for sonar job\n\n- SONAR_HOST_URL set to sonarcloud.io so sonarqube-scan-action targets the right host\n- replace SHA pins on sonar job actions with version tags to match the rest of the workflow\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(test): migrate node packages from Vitest to Rstest\n\nReplace Vitest with @rstest/core in contracts, db, env, and observability\npackages. Add @rstest/core to pnpm catalog. Drop test:coverage scripts\n(Rstest coverage support pending). Update all test file imports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIo7sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoL0QAJ1uooQ9u+bTIEtdpoRXfSCp\n8WTjvOPvGSGUbVvTv6QPpTs9biNcBomjxj+UpnTpL2vgi/ikYZ2qn2qFKUzMm0Fy\nZIVLywhyqvU9tj4i2a97JHCDAs8HBaKxlT0iuZJXRc7r83ycfqs9c9F5Mdacr/P/\nPRSUhMiHUTDiMZ8tRAmR9MrgjTRbD5hPNfv2xOW8UpLXF4MX0zXfmQAAbnCSqtJi\nt0jd2dyIl7ukGdtNg3lM6cTTcsCeZmCH6SvUUnAyWpLBQV+yTRC2zD4QvnjsshJp\nAAUHAx7zKv9qPMEXoMrTeZIpNU6eG8TlW4gyc9qGmp6dOf0kXZKkDHXiU6Qhlvu6\nKp/gSbK+ZaiRL4BZ9TqfBjCeeQE2u4XIrvGok3RF8+qoiH5NCEWkexc9k06anA3y\nlRjbt5zQa83GezEwaH7BbPCEvvRKTzAAZPdFm+B7OnFNXOQej2yJeIVBiDwOBTVn\n2yI0UB4A2o4dn5+1of4/BZ0WP4zfFKT+IGdGfodAlKMkmz6tLBzmwGz0mkXNflvd\nKlwlQ6LxT1eHMKIFrqAVEsvcKvTvEEqzjnNLbwpj75vutC/H7jubH0wUmj