"https://api.github.com/users/asmitdash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmitdash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmitdash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmitdash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmitdash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/asmitdash/CVS/commits/69dbccc9730ab0edc90d712cbe4d293470617612/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T06:47:10Z","email":"asmitdash44@gmail.com","name":"asmitdash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T06:47:10Z","email":"asmitdash44@gmail.com","name":"asmitdash"},"message":"feat(cvs): family relationship resolution for KYC-vs-RC mismatch\n\nAdds a deterministic resolver that infers the relationship between the\nclaimant and the master-record holder using Indian KYC kinship markers\n(S/O, W/O, D/O, H/O), father''s-name reciprocity on PAN/DL, and shared\naddress signals. Resolves the headline cases where a spouse claims on\nthe other spouse''s RC, or loyalty earned on one vehicle is consumed on\na second vehicle bought in the spouse''s name.\n\n- server/services/familyRelationResolver.js + relationshipUtils.js\n- server/services/ruleEvaluator.js: new family_linked operator\n- server/models/Rule.js: family_linked added to op enum\n- SalesRecord/RTORecord: relationshipVerdict field\n- auditPipeline.controller.js: resolver runs before rule evaluation\n- client RelationshipBadge in RecordDetailDrawer with hover-evidence\n- 17 new tests (11 resolver + 6 operator), 27/27 npm test green\n- README: new \"Family Relationship Resolution\" section","tree":{"sha":"722df115e6c2ef365b8a8a9a27229b7a769d108e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/asmitdash/CVS/git/trees/722df115e6c2ef365b8a8a9a27229b7a769d108e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/asmitdash/CVS/git/commits/69dbccc9730ab0edc90d712cbe4d293470617612","verification":{"payload":null,"rea