ps://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ai/commit/7ab9a920282b452580312345409a613ed04ebe37","node_id":"C_kwDOSut_MtoAKDdhYjlhOTIwMjgyYjQ1MjU4MDMxMjM0NTQwOWE2MTNlZDA0ZWJlMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ai/commit/be9831facbecf0d6d9864d21cc083c55272c8f18","sha":"be9831facbecf0d6d9864d21cc083c55272c8f18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/commits/be9831facbecf0d6d9864d21cc083c55272c8f18"}],"sha":"7ab9a920282b452580312345409a613ed04ebe37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/commits/7ab9a920282b452580312345409a613ed04ebe37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/commits/be9831facbecf0d6d9864d21cc083c55272c8f18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T21:56:54Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T21:56:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gpu-host): env-tunable analysis timeout + live-path VAD on (gitops#3484) (#329)\n\nTwo field-reported quality roots, both config-plane:\n\n1. meeting-ai loader now accepts MAI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT. The Python field\n   request_timeout (ge=1, le=300) already read it via env_prefix; the\n   allowlist was the only gate, so the 60s default was effectively\n   hard-wired. Under GPU load long transcripts starve at 60s — on\n   2026-08-27 three recovered ready-events re-died on\n   processing_AnalysisTimeoutError (8 attempts each).\n\n2. start-live-stt.ps1 live-path VAD default flips to \"true\" (both the\n   pre-import seed and the post-import re-assert). With it off, Whisper\n   hallucinates Turkish subtitle credits (\"Çeviri ve Altyazı M.K.\") into\n   silent stretches — reported live on 2026-08-17. The final path already\n   ran VAD; the same Silero gate now protects the live stream.\n\nBoth files parse clean (pwsh AST). The Windows acceptance suite needs the\nGPU host itself (exact interpreter/task-ancestry assertions) and runs as\npart of the deploy chain, not on this workstation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b3a2bb0ba47002cd6e3c9d5f4650f0de4f49f126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/git/trees/b3a2bb0ba47002cd6e3c9d5f4650f0de4f49f126"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/git/commits/be9831facbecf0d6d9864d21cc083c55272c8f18","verification":{"payload":"tree b3a2bb0ba47002cd6e3c9d5f4650f0de4f49f126\nparent 8c143ddcff0c119c8bf071c820a2c3fe8f923d1f\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1787867814 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787867814 +0300\n\nfix(gpu-host): env-tunable analysis timeout + live-path VAD on (gitops#3484) (#329)\n\nTwo field-reported quality roots, both config-plane:\n\n1. meeting-ai loader now accepts MAI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT. The Python field\n   request_timeout (ge=1, le=300) already read it via env_prefix; the\n   allowlist was the only gate, so the 60s default was effectively\n   hard-wired. Under GPU load long transcripts starve at 60s — on\n   2026-08-27 three recovered ready-events re-died on\n   processing_AnalysisTimeoutError (8 attempts each).\n\n2. start-live-stt.ps1 live-path VAD default flips to \"true\" (both the\n   pre-import seed and the post-import re-assert). With it off, Whisper\n   hallucinates Turkish subtitle credits (\"Çeviri ve Altyazı M.K.\") into\n   silent stretches — reported live on 2026-08-17. The final path already\n   ran VAD; the same Silero gate now protects the live stream.\n\nBoth files parse clean (pwsh AST). The Windows acceptance suite needs the\nGPU host itself (exact interpreter/task-ancestry assertions) and runs as\npart of the deploy chain, not on this workstation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkLKmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX70QACoYsfZdMrwRVdBG8D8mjvee\nCWdv5V25zAqBDomrpegQwMLusIG6CtFPg7YGP/oiBOP0lxHwuVCb33o0Iq8C95I2\nBxnpRgliIJ1cQK/8CHd4lJb3cERZm7WoY5O3/r1TQ1Vvl55YJGxYKxh23t4bJ5A2\n86+h2/icAI0qfblkORdN0H59f6jMY3Lmn4xBqO4CJYSkjFk2XmwdXrNRLXfeg695\nqy5CkzuzR0Hv08wg+9n0q4XC4L9XmDWFLfE9UHRTiWT4rXAAl7d/rM4aqjgbk584\nOl+wuCfAD1rf0UN6vS7TXPi7QZW3tFtsyOKVmkVWfT++iUAQB21YjGv2MvbI/pYL\n1i0plMHlSVXb/HYmgC4gBoYEcYYT2ghquWpdxzUA4+yOdl/5Mr/nDuRy42QRPf6k\ntlTRWB2f8/b/CzefgD83WN9tIXb1qEZUqkdqO0oFBzOcR2DeBjrShwhmQVBzUUgd\n7XzKzfgILw6m+7JCc8INYl5pKK4vHYCkNDX5TsNoyCeJB38nhAArD38hrNeJrxGL\nCSLFMwtlTp9XlMoE6fh9hYHo6N+RTGyMFqQM5zEdUQM1FHDFtMOvpLMJN79WfVgB\nWp1dScZmFXNbg