ai/commit/cf582b35ca7fd46f1da582dfd6117a1ea883d661","sha":"cf582b35ca7fd46f1da582dfd6117a1ea883d661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/commits/cf582b35ca7fd46f1da582dfd6117a1ea883d661"}],"sha":"fae6643e3a250019e22e095fa2e8c50a5d72516d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/commits/fae6643e3a250019e22e095fa2e8c50a5d72516d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/commits/cf582b35ca7fd46f1da582dfd6117a1ea883d661/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T23:07:32Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T23:07:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(ci): path-filter service-tests matrix + 15m pytest timeout (kalıcı fix) (#269)\n\n* chore(ci): path-filter service-tests matrix + 15m pytest timeout\n\nSymptom: PR #268 stalled ~1.5h because the `live-stt-service` matrix\ncell hung during Whisper model download — a test suite the PR did not\ntouch. Cancelling produced a red bucket that blocked merge under the\nCI-red-block-merge rule.\n\nLong-term fix:\n\n1. `service-changes` job runs first, uses `dorny/paths-filter@v3` (pinned\n   by SHA) to detect which service subtrees the PR actually touched.\n   Also flags all four services on any `.github/workflows/ci.yml` change\n   so workflow edits keep running the full matrix.\n\n2. `service-tests` matrix now `needs` that filter and each cell has an\n   `if:` guard that stays true on non-PR events (main pushes still run\n   the full matrix; trunk baseline preserved) and only fires on PRs for\n   the touched service.\n\n3. `pytest (unit)` step wrapped in `timeout-minutes: 15` — a repeat of\n   the same hang can no longer sit for hours; it fails cleanly at the\n   15m mark with a real signal to investigate.\n\nGitHub Actions does not support dynamic-key `needs.X.outputs[matrix.foo]`\n(the output name must be a literal), so the `if:` enumerates each matrix\nvalue explicitly. Adding a new service means adding one filter block +\none `if:` clause — both trivial and visible in review.\n\nPost-merge behaviour on this same PR-shape: only `meeting-ai-service`\nruns; the other three cells show as skipped, not failed. CI wall time\ndrops from ~1.5h (hang) to ~2min for meeting-ai-only PRs.\n\nRef: platform-ai#268 (live-stt hang → agent-forced cancel).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): dynamic matrix — `matrix` context banned in job-level `if:`\n\nPrevious revision failed workflow parse: GitHub Actions expands the\nmatrix BEFORE the job-level `if:` is evaluated, so `matrix.service` is\nnot a valid context there (\"context ''matrix'' is not allowed here\" —\nactionlint + first CI run).\n\nSector-standard fix: dynamic matrix. The `service-changes` job now\noutputs a JSON array (`services`) that lists ONLY the services that\nshould run — the `service-tests` matrix is built from that array via\n`fromJSON`. On non-PR events (push, workflow_dispatch, schedule) all\nfour services are always emitted so trunk baseline stays complete.\n\nEmpty-array short-circuit: if a PR touched zero service subtrees the\n`service-tests` job skips entirely (needs.service-changes.outputs.services\n== ''[]''), keeping the CI status list clean.\n\nactionlint clean; no invalid-context errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"facec2569f9053b5a029fc67288506d0c057023b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/git/trees/facec2569f9053b5a029fc67288506d0c057023b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ai/git/commits/cf582b35ca7fd46f1da582dfd6117a1ea883d661","verification":{"payload":"tree facec2569f9053b5a029fc67288506d0c057023b\nparent 970e16f262d7e4e0d1fc03e236f58b41867b565e\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1784588852 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784588852 +0300\n\nchore(ci): path-filter service-tests matrix + 15m pytest timeout (kalıcı fix) (#269)\n\n* chore(ci): path-filter service-tests matrix + 15m pytest timeout\n\nSymptom: PR #268 stalled ~1.5h because the `live-stt-service` matrix\ncell hung during Whisper model download — a test suite the PR did not\ntouch. Cancelling produced a red bucket that blocked merge under the\nCI-red-block-merge rule.\n\nLong-term fix:\n\n1. `service-changes` job runs first, uses `dorny/paths-filter@v3` (pinned\n   by SHA) to detect which service subtrees the PR actually touched.\n   Also flags all four services on any `.github/workflows/ci.yml` change\n   so workflow edits keep running the full matrix.\n\n2. `service-tests` matrix now `needs` that filter and each cell has an\n   `if:` guard that stays true on non-PR events (main pushes still run\n   the full matrix; trunk baseline preserved) and only fires on PRs for\n   the touched service.\n\n3. `pytest (unit)` step wrapped in `timeout-minutes: 15` — a repeat of\n   the same hang can no longer sit for hours; it fails cleanly at the\n   15m mark with a real signal to investigate.\n\nGitHub Actions does not support dynamic-key `needs.X.outputs[matrix.foo]`\n(the output name must be a literal), so the `if:` enumerates each matrix\nvalue explicitly. Adding a new service means adding one filter block +\none `if:` clause — both trivial and visible in review.\n\nPost-merge behaviour on this same PR-shape: only `meeting-ai-service`\nruns; the other three cells show as skipped, not failed. CI wall time\ndrops from ~1.5h (hang) to ~2min for meeting-ai-only PRs.\n\nRef: platform-ai#268 (live-stt hang → agent-forced cancel).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): dynamic matrix — `matrix` context banned in job-level `if:`\n\nPrevious revision failed workflow parse: GitHub Actions expands the\nmatrix BEFORE the job-level `if:` is evaluated, so `matrix.service` is\nnot a valid context there (\"context ''matrix'' is not allowed here\" —\nactionlint + first CI run).\n\nSector-standard fix: dynamic matrix. The `service-changes` job now\noutputs a JSON array (`services`) that lists ONLY the services that\nshould run — the `service-tests` matrix is built from that array via\n`fromJSON`. On non-PR events (push, workflow_dispatch, schedule) all\nfour services are always emitted so trunk baseline stays complete.\n\nEmpty-array short-circuit: if a PR touched zero service subtrees the\n`service-tests` job skips entirely (needs.service-changes.outputs.services\n== ''[]''), keeping the CI status list clean.\n\nactionlint clean; no invalid-context errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXqo0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB9MQAGqGBsPEz4MLG4OZdAL9Em5p\nkOGRnhDWF29VQgikEjBy4zr/Zl+ZCKi5ySm917ZM2oEKfdnnevkMuIBhW09Hne5G\nvWdI8ly/m2yJJX2rc5w3qcG2Sw1tSFhRoxjbLYpR4heEu/kSh1cMn++eLhbTY9Bg\nBCAPd+ffpbTLLS5vDhJrmcgXTpEhq4WIPN0Q/Ykh9nLCQ